2 TYPE Military Service
2 NOTE Branch: ARMY
3 CONT Country: United States
3 CONT Conflict: World War I
3 CONT Unit: 102nd Engineer Regiment, 27th Infantry Division
3 CONT Dates: 1917–1919
3 CONT Awards: World War I Victory Medal
2 NOTE Served with the 102nd Engineer Regiment, 27th Infantry Division — a New York National Guard unit federalized in July 1917. Engagements included the East Poperinghe Line, the attacks on the Hindenburg 
3 CONC Line, the Allied advance through the Somme, the crossing of the Selle River, and action near Catillon and St. Souplet. Lifelong member of the Defendam Association of the 102nd Engineers, the regimenta
3 CONC l veterans' organization ("Defendam" being the 27th Division's Latin motto, from its 'Orion' shoulder patch). Postwar career: retired secretary of the Ken-Well Contracting Company and former president
3 CONC  of the Everett Transportation Company of Long Island City, Queens. Lived at 1107 North Avenue, New Rochelle; member of the Wykagyl Country Club, American Legion Post 8, the Elks, the Fathers Council 
3 CONC of Marymount College, and the Sons of Union Veterans of the Civil War. Married Marion Riordan (daughter of U.S. Representative Daniel J. Riordan) in 1924 at St. Patrick's Cathedral — the first wedding
3 CONC  officiated there by Patrick Cardinal Hayes after his elevation.
2 SOUR New York Times obituary, 24 Nov 1957 — "Edward Cranwell, a Retired Builder" (Special to The New York Times, New Rochelle, NY)
2 SOUR New York State Military Museum — 102nd Engineer Regiment unit history
2 SOUR Defendam Association of the 102nd Engineers (member)
