2 TYPE Military Service
2 NOTE Branch: ARMY
3 CONT Country: United States
3 CONT Conflict: World War II
3 CONT Rank: Staff Sergeant (S/SGT)
3 CONT Unit: 24th Medical Battalion, 24th Infantry Division
3 CONT Dates: Inducted 1 Sep 1942 — Discharged 14 Jan 1946
3 CONT Awards: Asiatic-Pacific Campaign Medal, World War II Victory Medal, American Campaign Medal, Philippine Liberation Medal, Good Conduct Medal
2 NOTE Pacific Theater combat medic with the 24th Infantry Division's medical battalion. Campaigns included New Guinea (Hollandia, Tanamerah Bay, Lake Sentani), and the Philippines (Leyte, Mindoro, Mindanao)
3 CONC . Assisted wounded or sick under enemy fire. Contracted dengue fever and other tropical diseases while serving in jungle conditions. The 24th Infantry Division earned five Pacific campaign streamers —
3 CONC  New Guinea (with Arrowhead), Leyte (with Arrowhead), Luzon, and Southern Philippines (with Arrowhead), plus Central Pacific — more than any other U.S. division in the Pacific. Oral history preserved 
3 CONC by the New York State Military Museum.
2 SOUR New York State Military Museum — Oral History Interview (Edward J. Crummey, Jr., 24th Medical Battalion)
2 SOUR 24th Infantry Division — official campaign credits (Central Pacific, New Guinea, Leyte, Luzon, Southern Philippines)
2 SOUR Republic of the Philippines — Philippine Liberation Medal (awarded to U.S. forces in the liberation campaign, Oct 1944–Sep 1945)
2 SOUR https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LKeV_Fv5kCo
2 SOUR https://museum.dmna.ny.gov/research/oral-history-project/oral-history-program-veteran-interviews-c
2 SOUR Find a Grave Memorial #192557611 (S SGT Edward J. Crummey II)
