2 TYPE Military Service
2 NOTE Branch: ARMY
3 CONT Country: United States
3 CONT Conflict: Korean War
3 CONT Rank: Medical Corpsman
3 CONT Unit: U.S. Army Medical Corps
3 CONT Dates: 1952–1954
3 CONT Awards: National Defense Service Medal, Korean Service Medal
2 NOTE Served as a U.S. Army Medical Corpsman from 1952 to 1954, spanning the final year of the Korean War (armistice signed 27 July 1953) and the immediate post-armistice occupation period. Born in Troy, NY
3 CONC  in 1930 to Walter J. Dugan Sr. and Dorothy Faden Dugan. After his service he earned a B.S. in pre-med from Siena College and an M.A. in advanced business management from RPI, retiring as Vice Preside
3 CONC nt of Marketing and Sales at Lydall, Manning Inc. in Green Island, NY. Also a self-employed technical and marketing consultant; chairman/vice-chairman of NEMA's Insulating Materials Division; member o
3 CONC f ASTM, INDA, and TAPPI; founding president of the Parish Council of St. Bonaventure's Church in Speigletown; member of the Rensselaer County Board of Sewer Commissioners during the planning and const
3 CONC ruction of the county's municipal sewer disposal plant.
2 SOUR Albany Times Union / Legacy.com obituary, 31 Aug 2016 — "Dugan, Raymond C.": https://www.legacy.com/us/obituaries/timesunion-albany/name/raymond-dugan-obituary?id=5015832
2 SOUR John J. Sanvidge Funeral Home, Troy, NY — services held 1 Sep 2016, interment St. John's Cemetery, Troy
1 EVEN
2 TYPE Affiliation
2 NOTE Siena College — B.S., Pre-Medicine
2 NOTE Earned a B.S. in pre-med from Siena College (Loudonville, NY) after his service in the U.S. Army Medical Corps during the Korean War.
