2 TYPE Military Service
2 NOTE Branch: NAVY
3 CONT Country: United States
3 CONT Conflict: World War II
3 CONT Rank: Engineering Officer
3 CONT Unit: USS LST-491 (Landing Ship, Tank)
3 CONT Dates: Enlisted 1942 — Discharged 1946
3 CONT Awards: European-African-Middle Eastern Campaign Medal, Asiatic-Pacific Campaign Medal, World War II Victory Medal, American Campaign Medal, Philippine Liberation Medal
2 NOTE Enlisted in the U.S. Navy in 1942 while studying engineering at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (later continued at Cornell). By 1943 was named Engineering Officer of USS LST-491, an LST (Landing Shi
3 CONC p, Tank) amphibious assault ship that saw extraordinary action across both major theaters of World War II. Aboard LST-491 he survived the invasion of Normandy in the European Theater, and subsequently
3 CONC  participated in operations in the Philippines and the invasions of Iwo Jima and Okinawa in the Pacific Theater. Discharged 1946. At LaSalle Institute of Troy he had been Colonel of the Cadet regiment
3 CONC . Postwar earned a master's in chemical engineering from RPI and made his career at General Electric (Silicone Products, then Lexan Polycarbonate Plastics), rising to General Manager and Vice Presiden
3 CONC t (1966–1983).
2 SOUR Troy Record obituary — Walter James Dugan (Dec 2013): https://www.troyrecord.com/obituaries/walter-james-dugan-salt-lake-city-ny/
2 SOUR Family record — noted by JG3 (May 2026)
