3 CONT Awards: European-African-Middle Eastern Campaign Medal, World War II Victory Medal, American Campaign Medal, Combat Infantryman Badge, Good Conduct Medal
2 NOTE Served with the 254th Infantry Regiment, 63rd Infantry Division ("Blood and Fire"). The division saw 119 days of combat in the European Theater across the Rhineland, Ardennes-Alsace, and Central Europ
3 CONC e campaigns. Returned from Europe after the war, departing Marseille, France from the St. Victoret Sub Arse. Subject of the "J W Faden WWII Hero" obituary in the Troy Record.
